==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ang|bʰruHg}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*brūkaną||to enjoy, use}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-||enjoy}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|brūka}}, {{cog|goh|brūhhan}} ({{cog|de|brauchen}}), {{cog|osx|brūkan}}, {{cog|dum|bruken}} (Dutch {{m|nl|gebruiken}}), {{cog|got|𐌱𐍂𐌿𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root was also the source of Latin {{m|la|fruor||enjoy}} and {{m|la|frūx||fruit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbruːkɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=brūcan}}

# to [[enjoy]], to make use of
# to [[digest]] food

